Queue: [60, null]
→ pop 60, level=[40,60], add nothing
Queue: [null]
→ pop null, list=[[10],[20,30],[40,60]], level=[]
Queue: []

Output: [[10], [20, 30], [40, 60]]

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Level Order Line by Line
Given root of a binary tree, return its level order traversal with each level in a separate list.

Examples:

Input: root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, N, N, N, N, N, 8]

        1
       / \
      2   3
     / \ / \
    4  5 6  7
            \
             8

Output: [[1], [2, 3], [4, 5, 6, 7], [8]]
Explanation: Level 0: [1], Level 1: [2,3], Level 2: [4,5,6,7], Level 3: [8]

Input: root = [10, 20, 30, 40, 60]

       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \ 
   40  60

Output: [[10], [20, 30], [40, 60]]
Explanation: Level 0: [10], Level 1: [20,30], Level 2: [40,60]

Constraints:
• 1 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 1000
• 0 ≤ node->data ≤ 100

